description:
This program searches for a target number `42` in an array. It should print `"Found at index: " + i` and stop immediately when found. If the target is not in the array after checking all elements, it should print `"Not Found"`. However, the current code has two bugs: it stops after checking only the first element, and risks an out-of-bounds error. Find the bugs and rebuild the corrected program.
```
public class LinearSearch {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int[] data = {10, 25, 42, 88, 99};
        int target = 42;
        boolean found = false;
        for (int i = 0; i <= data.length; i++) {
            if (data[i] == target) {
                System.out.println("Found at index: " + i);
                found = true;
            }
            break;
        }
        if (!found) {
            System.out.println("Not Found");
        }
    }
}
```
